---
import "../styles/global.css";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
const href = (path: string) => `${base}${path}` || "/";
const releaseUrl = "https://github.com/udhawan97/Nindova/releases/tag/v0.1.0";
const standaloneUrl = "https://github.com/udhawan97/Nindova/releases/download/v0.1.0/nindova-v0.1.0.html";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover" />
    <meta
      http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy"
      content="default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; connect-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; media-src 'self' blob:; font-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self'"
    />
    <meta name="description" content="Rasoi Pairs is Nindova's calm, bounded pair-removal game made from Indian kitchen forms." />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Nindova — Rasoi Pairs" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Find matching kitchen tiles. Let the board grow lighter. Leave when it closes." />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <link rel="icon" href={href("/favicon.svg")} type="image/svg+xml" />
    <title>Nindova — Rasoi Pairs</title>
  </head>
  <body class="landing">
    <header class="site-nav" aria-label="Primary navigation">
      <a class="brand" href={href("/")} aria-label="Nindova home">
        <span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>Nindova</span>
      </a>
      <nav>
        <a href={href("/docs/")}>Docs</a>
        <a href={releaseUrl}>v0.1.0</a>
        <a class="nav-play" href={href("/play/")}>Play this build</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section class="rasoi-hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">A small kitchen for the end of the day</p>
          <h1 id="hero-title">Find the pairs.<br />Let the kitchen quiet.</h1>
          <p class="hero-lede">
            Rasoi Pairs is a calm 36-tile game inspired by Mahjong solitaire. Match familiar Indian
            kitchen forms at the open ends of three racks. The board gets lighter, then the Session ends.
          </p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button-primary" href={href("/play/")}>Play Rasoi Pairs</a>
            <a class="button-secondary" href={standaloneUrl}>Download standalone</a>
          </div>
          <p class="trust-line">Nothing to win. Nothing tracked. Nothing you can do wrong.</p>
        </div>

        <figure class="hero-board">
          <div class="board-frame">
            <img
              src={href("/media/rasoi-board.png")}
              width="840"
              height="384"
              alt="The real Rasoi Pairs board with three shallow racks; exposed matching tiles are bright at each end."
            />
          </div>
          <figcaption>Rendered from the release Session · no concept mockup</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <div class="motif-line" aria-label="Kitchen motifs in Rasoi Pairs">
          <span>Belan</span><span>Chakla</span><span>Tawa</span><span>Chimta</span><span>Katori</span><span>Tiffin</span><span>Masala dabba</span><span>Chai</span><span>Cooker</span>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="rule-section" aria-labelledby="rule-title">
        <div class="rule-intro">
          <p class="eyebrow">One rule, all night</p>
          <h2 id="rule-title">Easy to understand.<br />Impossible to spoil.</h2>
          <p>
            A tile is free when it sits at an exposed rack end. Choose two free tiles showing the same
            object. Every legal choice on the authored board keeps a path to the ending.
          </p>
        </div>
        <ol class="rule-steps">
          <li><span aria-hidden="true">01</span><div><h3>Look</h3><p>The brighter edge tiles are free.</p></div></li>
          <li><span aria-hidden="true">02</span><div><h3>Pair</h3><p>Belan with belan. Chai with chai.</p></div></li>
          <li><span aria-hidden="true">03</span><div><h3>Settle</h3><p>The pair lifts, sounds once if enabled, and leaves.</p></div></li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="material-section" aria-labelledby="material-title">
        <figure class="phone-art">
          <div class="phone-frame">
            <img
              src={href("/media/rasoi-pairs-phone.png")}
              width="375"
              height="815"
              alt="The real Rasoi Pairs phone layout, with labeled kitchen tiles and a safe-pair help control."
            />
          </div>
          <figcaption>375px release surface</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <div class="material-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Punjabi material, everyday kitchen</p>
          <h2 id="material-title">Indigo cloth. Madder thread. Steel and brass.</h2>
          <p>
            The visual system draws from Punjabi material craft without turning it into decoration for
            decoration's sake. Restrained phulkari-inspired geometry frames ordinary kitchen forms; the
            object name remains visible so recognition never depends on illustration alone.
          </p>
          <dl class="material-ledger">
            <div><dt>Palette</dt><dd>Indigo, madder, marigold, cream, brass</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Objects</dt><dd>Everyday cooking and tea forms</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Excluded</dt><dd>Flags, sacred symbols, festival collage</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <p class="honesty-note">Punjabi-inspired direction; completed human cultural-authenticity review is not claimed.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="boundary-section" aria-labelledby="boundary-title">
        <header>
          <p class="eyebrow">A game with an exit</p>
          <h2 id="boundary-title">Satisfaction stays inside the Session.</h2>
        </header>
        <div class="boundary-grid">
          <div>
            <h3>While you play</h3>
            <p>Predictable lift, one restrained clack, a warmer open rack. Help points; it never plays.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>When it ends</h3>
            <p>No score, timer, streak, grade, collection, randomized reward, or promoted replay.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>If you leave it</h3>
            <p>The kitchen settles itself before the hidden fifteen-minute ceiling. The ending stays the same.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="dawn-section" aria-labelledby="dawn-title">
        <div class="dawn-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Morning, only if you return</p>
          <h2 id="dawn-title">First light keeps the forms, not the result.</h2>
          <p>
            From 06:00 through 11:59 in the captured Night ID zone, Dawn rearranges last night's kitchen
            forms as a quiet local still. Save it, make a subtle silent loop, or leave it there. No notification asks you back.
          </p>
        </div>
        <figure class="dawn-art">
          <img
            src={href("/media/rasoi-dawn.png")}
            width="712"
            height="452"
            alt="The real Dawn canvas: nine kitchen forms resting on brass plates in warm first light."
          />
          <figcaption>Rendered Dawn canvas · local export surface</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="trust-section" aria-labelledby="trust-title">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">The technical promise</p>
          <h2 id="trust-title">Your night stays on your device.</h2>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>No account</strong><span>Open the file or PWA and begin.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Zero telemetry</strong><span>No analytics, ads, or remote logging.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Offline-ready</strong><span>Installable PWA plus a standalone HTML.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Accessible rule</strong><span>Native buttons, 44px targets, keyboard, reduced motion, and visible names.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="closing-section" aria-labelledby="closing-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Release v0.1.0</p>
        <h2 id="closing-title">One board. One ending.</h2>
        <p>
          Nindova is a behavioral design study, not a sleep tracker or treatment. Rasoi Pairs has not
          been clinically shown to make people sleepy or improve sleep.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button-primary" href={href("/play/")}>Play this build</a>
          <a class="button-secondary" href={releaseUrl}>Release notes and checksums</a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer">
      <a class="brand" href={href("/")}><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Nindova</span></a>
      <nav aria-label="Footer navigation">
        <a href={href("/docs/")}>Documentation</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/udhawan97/Nindova">GitHub</a>
        <a href={releaseUrl}>v0.1.0</a>
      </nav>
      <p>Behavioral design study · 13+ · no public web deployment</p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
